      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily looks like a dosing error, so I want to check with you first.\n\n**The problem:**\n- The usual adult dose of amlodipine is 2.5\u201310 mg by mouth once daily.\n- The maximum recommended dose is 10 mg/day. 50 mg is 5 times that.\n- At that dose there's a real risk of severe low blood pressure, reflex tachycardia, and distributive shock. Amlodipine overdose can be prolonged and hard to treat.\n\n**Possible typo:** Did you mean **5 mg** once daily? That's a common starting dose and fits an adult with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nPlease confirm the dose you want:\n1. **Amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**, or\n2. Another dose within 2.5\u201310 mg, or\n3. If you really do mean 50 mg, tell me the clinical reason. I'd also recommend checking with pharmacy before it's entered.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter the order."
      }
     ],
