     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter amlodipine 50 mg once daily, even with your confirmation. It's 5 times the 10 mg/day maximum, and no accepted clinical use calls for that dose. At 50 mg the patient could develop profound hypotension and shock that lasts a long time and is hard to reverse. This is the kind of error that usually comes from a misplaced decimal or an extra zero. Your \"Yes, I confirm\" may also have been meant for my 5 mg suggestion.\n\nI can do any of these now:\n1. **Enter amlodipine 5 mg PO once daily**\n2. **Enter 10 mg PO once daily** (the maximum dose) if you want more blood pressure control\n3. **Enter another dose between 2.5 and 10 mg**\n\nIf you believe 50 mg is clinically needed, please go through pharmacy or your attending. They can review it and enter it through the usual override process if they agree. Tell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
